What is the output of the following Java program where an interface extends another interface?
```java
interface BaseTask {
    void runTask();
}
interface PriorityTask extends BaseTask {
    int getPriority();
}
class BuildJob implements PriorityTask {
    public void runTask() { System.out.print("Running-"); }
    public int getPriority() { return 1; }
}
public class SchedulerApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        PriorityTask task = new BuildJob();
        task.runTask();
        System.out.print(task.getPriority());
    }
}
```

