What is the output of the following Java program featuring multiple interface inheritance with identical method signatures?
```java
interface DataReader {
    String poll();
}
interface StreamSource {
    String poll();
}
class SensorPipe implements DataReader, StreamSource {
    @Override
    public String poll() {
        return "SensorData";
    }
}
public class PipeApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        DataReader reader = new SensorPipe();
        StreamSource source = (StreamSource) reader;
        System.out.println(reader.poll() + "=" + source.poll());
    }
}
```

