What is the output of the following Java program combining interface constant inheritance and field hiding in the implementing class?
```java
interface Protocol {
    int VERSION = 1;
}
class SecureProtocol implements Protocol {
    public static int VERSION = 2;
    public void show() {
        System.out.print(VERSION + ":" + Protocol.VERSION);
    }
}
public class ProtocolApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new SecureProtocol().show();
    }
}
```
